# Cursor skills — dual location sync

When **creating**, **updating**, or **moving** an Excelsior agent skill, **always write both copies** in the same change — do not wait for the user to ask.

## Locations (keep identical content, path-aware)

| Copy | Root |
|------|------|
| **Repo** (versioned, shared) | `.cursor/skills/{skill-name}/` |
| **Global** (user machine) | `C:\Users\Kyle\.cursor\skills\{skill-name}/` |

Mirror the full skill folder: `SKILL.md`, companion docs (`PATH_RULES.md`, etc.), and `scripts/` when present.

## Path conventions in SKILL.md

Script and helper paths **differ by copy** — adjust when syncing:

| Copy | Script invocation example |
|------|---------------------------|
| Repo | `& ".cursor/skills/pdf-to-png/scripts/Convert-PdfToPng.ps1"` |
| Global | `& "C:\Users\Kyle\.cursor\skills\pdf-to-png\scripts\Convert-PdfToPng.ps1"` |

Repo-relative links to project docs (`docs/`, `migrations/`, etc.) stay as-is in **both** copies.

## Workflow

1. Edit or create the skill in **both** locations before reporting done.
2. If only one location exists, create the missing mirror immediately.
3. On update, diff mentally: same behavior, only path roots differ where needed.
4. Tell the user which files were updated in each location.

## In scope

Excelsior workflow skills under `.cursor/skills/` (e.g. `add-card`, `ship`, `pdf-to-png`, `start-aws-db-tunnel`).

## Out of scope

- `C:\Users\Kyle\.cursor\skills-cursor\` — Cursor product skills; do not duplicate into the repo.
- Skills with no Excelsior tie-in unless the user explicitly asks to add them to the repo.
